---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Layout title="Why is the unauthorized user still hitting your action?" description="Practice card. A before_action that looks like it should block, but doesn't. Drills the halting rule.">
  <article class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 space-y-6">
    <div>
      <a href="/" class="text-ruby hover:text-ruby-dark transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-2 mb-6">
        <span>←</span> Back to Course
      </a>
      <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-ruby font-semibold mb-2">Practice · Reading the Source · Card 4</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-ruby-dark mb-4">Why is the unauthorized user still hitting your action?</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">A <code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded text-base">before_action</code> that reads like it should block non-admins. It doesn't. The bug is one missing call.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-start">
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200 p-8 space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-gray-500">🔍</span> The code
          </h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 italic mb-3">A non-admin can call <code>destroy</code>. The before_action runs, but doesn't stop them.</p>
          <div class="border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-gray-50/40">
            <CodeBlock code={`class PostsController < ApplicationController
  before_action :require_admin, only: [:destroy]

  def destroy
    @post = Post.find(params[:id])
    @post.destroy
    redirect_to posts_path
  end

  private

  def require_admin
    flash[:alert] = "Admins only" unless current_user.admin?
  end
end`} language="ruby" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">The question</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A regular user calls <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">DELETE /posts/42</code>. The <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">require_admin</code> callback runs. The post still gets destroyed. <strong>What rule did this controller break?</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200 p-8 space-y-6 lg:sticky lg:top-6">
        <div id="prompt-section" class="space-y-6">
          <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-7">
            <p class="text-base text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              <strong>Take a moment.</strong> Rails halts the callback chain when a specific condition is met. Setting <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">flash[:alert]</code> isn't that condition. What is?
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="pt-2">
            <button
              id="show-solution-btn"
              class="w-full px-6 py-3 bg-ruby text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-ruby-dark transition-colors font-medium"
            >
              Reveal the answer →
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="solution-section" class="hidden space-y-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-green-600">✅</span> The answer
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>The callback never set a response, so Rails ran the action anyway.</strong> Rails halts the chain only when a before_action calls <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">render</code>, <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">redirect_to</code>, or throws <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">:abort</code>. Setting <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">flash[:alert]</code> mutates the session, but doesn't tell Rails "stop the chain." The fix:</p>
            <div class="border-2 border-green-200 rounded-lg p-4 bg-green-50/30">
              <CodeBlock code={`def require_admin
  unless current_user.admin?
    flash[:alert] = "Admins only"
    redirect_to root_path   # <-- this is what halts the chain
  end
end

# Now:
#   non-admin hits DELETE /posts/42
#   require_admin runs → redirect_to root_path
#   Rails sees response is set → chain halts
#   destroy action is SKIPPED
#   user lands on root_path with the flash`} language="ruby" />
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>💡</span> The halting rule
            </h3>
            <div class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
              <p>Rails checks one thing between callbacks: <strong>has a response been set?</strong> If yes, the chain halts and the action is skipped. If no, the chain keeps going. That's the entire rule.</p>
              <p>Calling <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">render</code> or <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">redirect_to</code> sets the response. Setting <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">flash</code>, mutating instance variables, logging, or returning <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">false</code> from the callback does not. This is the most common authorization bug shape in Rails: a callback that "looks" like it blocks, but only mutates state.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>📚</span> Theory
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">For the full walkthrough of <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">before_action</code> chains and halting, read <a href="/lessons/source-before-action" class="text-ruby hover:text-ruby-dark font-medium">Card 6 of Reading the Source</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-between items-center pt-4">
      <a href="/lessons/practice-source-require-vs-bracket" class="text-ruby hover:text-ruby-dark transition-colors">← Card 3</a>
      <a href="/lessons/practice-source-raw-form-missing" class="text-ruby hover:text-ruby-dark transition-colors">Card 5 →</a>
    </div>
  </article>

  <script>
    const btn = document.getElementById('show-solution-btn');
    const prompt = document.getElementById('prompt-section');
    const solution = document.getElementById('solution-section');
    if (btn && prompt && solution) {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        prompt.classList.add('hidden');
        solution.classList.remove('hidden');
        if (window.innerWidth < 1024) {
          solution.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
        }
      });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
